Ta có:
\cos\left(2x - $\frac{\pi}{3}$\$right) = \frac{1}{2}$\Leftrightarrow \cos\left(2x -$\frac{\pi}{3}$\right) = \cos\frac{\pi}{3}
\Leftrightarrow \left[\begin{aligned} 2x - $\frac{\pi}{3}$ &= $\frac{\pi}{3}$ + k2\pi \\ 2x - $\frac{\pi}{3}$ &= -$\frac{\pi}{3}$ + k2\pi \end{aligned}\right. \Leftrightarrow \left[\begin{aligned} 2x &= $\frac{2\pi}{3}$ + k2\pi \\ 2x &= k2\pi \end{aligned}\right. \Leftrightarrow \left[\begin{aligned} x &= $\frac{\pi}{3}$ + k\pi \\ x &= k\pi \end{aligned}\right. \quad (k \in \mathbb{Z})

